 "standard_url": "https://www.education.gov.za/Portals/0/CD/National%20Curriculum%20Statements%20and%20Vocational/CAPS%20FET%20_%20MATHEMATICS%20_%20GR%2010-12%20_%20Web_1133.pdf",
 "standard_text": "Definition of a logarithm: y = log<sub>b</sub> x ⟺ x = bʸ (b &gt; 0, b ≠ 1, x &gt; 0); the graph of the inverse of y = bˣ; use logarithms to solve exponential equations (for example, finding n in financial calculations).",
 "meta_desc": "Free CAPS Grade 12 logarithms worksheets: the definition of a log, log laws, solving exponential equations and the graph of y = log x. 100 questions with memos.",
 "key_big": "log of x to base b = y means bʸ = x.",
 "key_sub": "bˣ = k gives x = log k ÷ log b.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How to think about it</h2><ul><li>y = log<sub>b</sub> x means bʸ = x (b &gt; 0, b ≠ 1, x &gt; 0).</li><li>Log laws: log(ab) = log a + log b, log(a ÷ b) = log a − log b, log aⁿ = n log a.</li><li>To solve bˣ = k, take logs: x = <span class='fr'><span class='fn'>log k</span><span class='fd'>log b</span></span>.</li><li>y = log<sub>b</sub> x passes through (1; 0) and has the asymptote x = 0.</li></ul><h2>Examples</h2><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>2ˣ = 20</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>x = log 20 ÷ log 2</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: x = 4,32</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>What to do instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>log(a + b)</td><td>There is no law for a sum inside the log.</td></tr><tr><td>The base</td><td>log₂ 8 = 3 because 2³ = 8.</td></tr><tr><td>Dividing numbers</td><td>x = log 20 ÷ log 2, not 20 ÷ 2.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
 "faq": [
  {
   "q": "What does CAPS Grade 12 say?",
   "a": "Know the definition of a logarithm and the graph of y = log<sub>b</sub> x as the inverse of y = bˣ, and use logs to solve exponential equations, including in finance."
  },
  {
   "q": "What is log 1?",
   "a": "0."
  },
  {
   "q": "Can you take the log of a negative number?",
   "a": "No."
  },
  {
   "q": "What base does log mean?",
   "a": "Base 10."
  }
